        "subject": "LU-20911 lov: rebuild EC stripes with no object from parity",
        "message": "LU-20911 lov: rebuild EC stripes with no object from parity\n\nA read of an EC file failed with -EIO if a data stripe had no\nobject, as for the dummy slot that LFSCK leaves in a layout for a\nlost OST object, although the parity of its raid set could rebuild\nthe stripe as it does for an unavailable OST.\n\nSwitch such a read to CIT_EC_RD in lov_io_iter_init(), except for AIO,\nwhose earlier chunks may still be in flight, and count the stripe as\nlost in lov_ecio_add_data_sub(), with a debug message rather than a\nconsole warning, so that parity rebuilds it into pages with no\nsub-object (lov_page_init_composite()).  No lock covers these pages,\nso they are kept only until the layout lock is cancelled, which any\nchange of the data does first.  A stripe with no object in a component\nwithout parity, a write and a fault still fail.\n\nUse OBD_FAIL_MAKE_LOVEA_HOLE, which was never used so far, to clear\nthe objects on the OSTs that fail_val selects (cfs_fail_index()) when\nthe client unpacks a layout, and add sanity-ec test_45a to read an EC\nfile with no object for its first data stripe.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-ec\nFixes: 783c13bb0b8f (\"LU-12669 ec: recover data from parity\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I3c4e842683ea720ad6140f9d918b07a62f3ebbe5\n"
      },
